one oxidoreductase; Does not have alcohol dehydrogenase activity. Binds NADP and acts through a one-electron transfer process. Orthoquinones, such as 1,2-naphthoquinone or 9,10-phenanthrenequinone, are the best substrates (in vitro). May act in the detoxification of xenobiotics. Interacts with (AU)-rich elements (ARE) in the 3'-UTR of target mRNA species. Enhances the stability of mRNA coding for BCL2. NADPH binding interferes with mRNA binding."},{"po":105762,"n":"tissue::thyroid gland","v":"2.289761","d":"double"},{"po":105762,"n":"display name","v":"CRYZ"},{"po":105762,"n":"tissue::adrenal gland","v":"2.471495","d":"double"},{"po":105762,"n":"tissue::gall bladder","v":"2.218036","d":"double"},{"po":105762,"n":"log2FoldChange","v":"-1.728493033344059","d":"double"},{"po":105762,"n":"stringdb::sequence","v":""},{"po":105762,"n":"tissue::intestine","v":"2.924496","d":"double"},{"po":105762,"n":"stringdb::node color","v":"rgb(117,205,239)"},{"po":105762,"n":"stringdb::database identifier","v":"9606.ENSP00000399805"},{"po":105762,"n":"tissue::blood","v":"3.047227","d":"double"},{"po":105762,"n":"tissue::spleen","v":"2.271539","d":"double"},{"po":105759,"n":"stringdb::namespace","v":"stringdb"},{"po":105759,"n":"tissue::urine","v":"1.090909","d":"double"},{"po":105759,"n":"compartment::nucleus","v":"4.771024","d":"double"},{"po":105759,"n":"stringdb::structures","v":["6z2k_F","AF-Q6PJG2"],"d":"list_of_string"},{"po":105759,"n":"tissue::saliva","v":"0.78295","d":"double"},{"po":105759,"n":"stringdb::species","v":"Homo sapiens"},{"po":105759,"n":"tissue::liver","v":"4.176921","d":"double"},{"po":105759,"n":"compartment::extracellular","v":"0.526028","d":"double"},{"po":105759,"n":"tissue::stomach","v":"1.090909","d":"double"},{"po":105759,"n":"tissue::bone marrow","v":"1.069421","d":"double"},{"po":105759,"n":"tissue::heart","v":"1.342958","d":"double"},{"po":105759,"n":"stringdb::enhancedLabel Passthrough","v":"label: attribute=\"display name\" labelsize=12 labelAlignme