"},{"po":105750,"n":"tissue::lung","v":"1.805745","d":"double"},{"po":105750,"n":"compartment::cytosol","v":"1.953262","d":"double"},{"po":105750,"n":"tissue::skin","v":"1.637303","d":"double"},{"po":105750,"n":"query term","v":"GRIK1"},{"po":105750,"n":"gene_symbol","v":"GRIK1"},{"po":105750,"n":"pvalue","v":"1.443914441851329E-5","d":"double"},{"po":105750,"n":"compartment::plasma membrane","v":"4.769487","d":"double"},{"po":105750,"n":"stringdb::imageurl","v":"https://version-12-0.string-db.org//images/Proteinpictures/pdb/7l/7lvt_A.png"},{"po":105750,"n":"tissue::kidney","v":"1.961992","d":"double"},{"po":105750,"n":"baseMean","v":"303.8547654104604","d":"double"},{"po":105750,"n":"@id","v":"stringdb:9606.ENSP00000327687"},{"po":105750,"n":"compartment::endoplasmic reticulum","v":"2.235774","d":"double"},{"po":105750,"n":"stringdb::description","v":"Glutamate receptor ionotropic, kainate 1; Ionotropic glutamate receptor. L-glutamate acts as an excitatory neurotransmitter at many synapses in the central nervous system. Binding of the excitatory neurotransmitter L-glutamate induces a conformation change, leading to the opening of the cation channel, and thereby converts the chemical signal to an electrical impulse. The receptor then desensitizes rapidly and enters a transient inactive state, characterized by the presence of bound agonist. May be involved in the transmission of light information from the retina to the hypothalamus."},{"po":105750,"n":"tissue::thyroid gland","v":"1.889685","d":"double"},{"po":105750,"n":"display name","v":"GRIK1"},{"po":105750,"n":"tissue::adrenal gland","v":"2.01004","d":"double"},{"po":105750,"n":"tissue::gall bladder","v":"0.545455","d":"double"},{"po":105750,"n":"log2FoldChange","v":"-1.1702707370427847","d":"double"},{"po":105750,"n":"stringdb::sequence","v":""},{"po":105750,"n":"tissue::intestine","v":"1.967697","d":"double"},{"po":105750,"n":"stringdb::node color","v":"rgb(117,239,137)"},{"po":105750,"n":"stringdb::database id